-0579.2000.040204.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Career preferences of doctors</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1996</year><volume>313</volume><fpage>2</fpage><lpage>2</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8664764</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Factors affecting career choices in medicine</article-title><source>Best Practice &#x00026; Research in Clinical Obstetrics &#x00026; Gynaecology</source><year>1999</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>323</fpage><lpage>330</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1053/beog.1999.0028</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Allen</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Modernising the NHS - Challenges to the health services: the professions</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>2000</year><volume>320</volume><fpage>1533</fpage><lpage>1535</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10834906</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1136/bmj.320.7248.1533</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldacre</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Planning the United Kingdom's medical workforce</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1998</year><volume>316</volume><fpage>1846</fpage><lpage>1847</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9632401</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Department of Health</collab></person-group><source>Primary Care Workforce Review</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name> London: Department of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>NHS Scotland</collab></person-group><source>An update on the analysis and modelling of the dental workforce in Scotland</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name> NHS Scotland</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Seward</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>McEwen</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Provision of Dental-Care by Women Dentists in England and Wales in 1985 - a 10-Year Review</article-title><source>British Dental Journal</source><year>1987</year><volume>162</volume><fpage>50</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3468961</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/sj.bdj.4806020</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B33"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Secretary of State for Health</collab></person-group><source>Reforms with bite &#x02013; 1000 more dentists by October 2005</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>London , Department of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B34"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>The Information Centre</collab></person-group><source>NHS Dental Activity and Workforce Report England 31 March 2006</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name> London: Department of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B35"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Chief Dental Officer</collab></person-group><source>NHS Dentistry: delivering change</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name> London: Department of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B36"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><colla